; 23-mode.kurt

; Every open block has a "mode": `root`, `sandbox`, `proof`, `assume` (also
; used for `case`), `let`, `pick`, or `expect` (16-expect.kurt) -- it's
; simply which keyword opened the block you are currently in.  `mode`
; prints the mode of the current level.

; Running a *file* actually starts one level deep already, inside an implicit
; `sandbox` (the same mechanism `load`, lesson 10, uses to keep a failed file
; from half-loading) -- so even here, at the top, `mode` won't say "root":
mode

bool A, B
use A implies B

show A implies B "demo"
proof
    mode          ; now inside the `proof` block
    assume A
        mode      ; now inside the nested `assume` block
        use B
qed
